F_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "Fixes the nightly failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` was documented as banker's rounding per FIN-212 but used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. This switches it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which the existing test expects (2.675 -> 2.68, 2.665 -> 2.66).\n\nCI: passed on 08d3cd5986 (ci-0001).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-bankers-rounding-pr"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is up as PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer. I have not merged it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101", "type": "text"}]}]}